\section*{Higher Verlinde fiber functors in positive characteristic}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. Every finite symmetric tensor category in characteristic $p>0$ is claimed to admit an exact faithful symmetric tensor functor to a finite higher Verlinde category, including at $p=2$.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Result 1.} For each prime \(p\), algebraically closed characteristic-\(p\) field \(k\), and finite symmetric tensor category \(\mathcal C\) over \(k\), the claim supplies an integer \(n\ge1\) and an exact faithful symmetric tensor functor
\[
 \mathcal C\longrightarrow\operatorname{Ver}_{p^n}(k).
\]
The target is the higher Verlinde category at level \(p^n\); the level may depend on \(\mathcal C\), rather than being a universal fixed choice.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
A representation-theoretic restricted-tilting assertion supplies the higher Frobenius construction. Classification and reconstruction then identify a suitable finite level of the Verlinde tower and produce the faithful fiber functor; the tower level can vary with the input category.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The proposed functor is faithful and exact, respects the symmetric tensor structure, and is linear over the chosen coefficient field. Every finite category in the stated positive-characteristic class is assigned some finite Verlinde level, with no fixed uniform level required. This is presented as a claimed affirmative answer.

